  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "What are the sum and product, respectively, of the two roots of \\(x²-5x+6=0\\)? (Answer in order, separated by a comma.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "5，6",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(a=1\\), \\(b=-5\\), and \\(c=6\\). The sum of the two roots is \\(-b/a=5\\), and their product is \\(c/a=6\\). (This can also be verified by directly finding the roots \\(2\\) and \\(3\\).)\n\nAlternative method 1: Find the roots by factoring\n\nFactoring finds the roots themselves:\n\\[\nx^2-5x+6=(x-2)(x-3).\n\\]\nThe product is zero exactly when \\(x=2\\) or \\(x=3\\). Their sum and product, in the requested order, are \\(2+3=5\\) and \\(2\\cdot3=6\\).",
